phi-adapter-thinq (0.1.3-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Acknowledge the appliance's frames the way the cloud does (`ack`
    command, F0 00 <type> 04, plus the sequence for envelopes); answer
    req_timesync with the seven UTC bytes; send a dishwasher the start
    packet after provisioning; note an undeploy. Without the acks a freshly
    enrolled D0211 repeated its identification record and undeployed after
    a few minutes, its Wi-Fi LED dark.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:52:32 +0000

phi-adapter-thinq (0.1.2-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * phi-thinq-routed no longer mints a CA of its own: it signs with the box
    CA phi-mosquitto keeps under /var/lib/phi/tls (--ca-dir, PHI_TLS_DIR)
    and re-issues its own leaf when that CA or the host name changes. The
    8883 listener lives in phi-mosquitto's drop-in now; the example drop-in
    is gone, and the package recommends phi-mosquitto rather than mosquitto.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:20:00 +0200

phi-adapter-thinq (0.1.1-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The broker account is read from the adapter record, where the intent
    rule puts it; the form's fields override.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Sun, 19 Oct 2026 14:50:00 +0200

phi-adapter-thinq (0.1.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First scaffold of the local ThinQ adapter: AABB framing, the MQTT
    envelope and provisioning answer, washer commands and vocabulary, status
    decoders on the unverified F_V8 and D0211 tables, one phi device per
    appliance; phi-thinq-routed with the box CA, /route and CSR signing;
    example mosquitto and dnsmasq drop-ins.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Sun, 19 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0200
